<title>AUSTRALIA: TENNIS-AUSTRALIAN OPEN RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-AUSTRALIAN OPEN RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results on the fifth day of the US$7.6 million Australian Open tennis tournament on Friday (prefix denotes seeding):</p>
<p>Men's singles, third round:</p>
<p>Carlos Moya (Spain) beat Bernd Karbacher (Germany) 6-2 6-2 6-2</p>
<p>9-Marcelo Rios (Chile) beat Gilbert Schaller (Austria) 4-6 7-6 (7-2) 6-1 6-1</p>
<p>Jonas Bjorkman (Sweden) beat Karsten Braasch (Germany) 6-4 7-6 (7-5) 6-3</p>
<p>MaliVai Washington (U.S.) beat Todd Woodbridge (Australia) 4-6 6-2 6-3 6-1</p>
<p>Women's singles, third round</p>
<p>5-Anke Huber (Germany) beat Natasha Zvereva (Belarus) 7-5 6-0</p>
<p>7-Lindsay Davenport (U.S.) beat Tamarine Tanasugarn (Thailand) 6-1 6-0</p>
<p>1-Steffi Graf (Germany) beat Ines Gorrochategui (Argentina) 7-5 6-3</p>
<p>12-Amanda Coetzer (South Africa) beat Maria Luisa Serna (Spain) 6-3 6-2</p>
<p>Kimberly Po (U.S.) beat Rika Hiraki (Japan) 6-2 6-2  </p>
<p>Add men's results:</p>
<p>Andrei Medvedev (Ukraine) beat Dennis van Scheppingen (Netherlands) 6-1 6-1 6-1</p>
<p>14-Felix Mantilla (Spain) beat Arnaud Boetsch (France) 6-3 1-6 7-6 (7-4) 6-4</p>
<p>Add women's singles:</p>
<p>Mary Pierce (France) beat Marketa Kochta (Germany) 6-0 6-2</p>
<p>16-Sabine Appelmans (Belgium) beat Kristie Boogert</p>
<p>(Netherlands) 6-1 3-1 (retired)</p>
<p>Add men's singles, third round</p>
<p>7-Thomas Enqvist (Sweden) beat Sergi Bruguera (Spain) 7-6 (10-8) 7-5 6-2</p>
</text>
